# Xcode project file — generated from project.yml by XcodeGen.
# Regenerate with `xcodegen generate` after cloning or after any project.yml
# change. Committing the raw .xcodeproj is the single biggest cause of
# needless merge conflicts in iOS repos (it's an internal, auto-managed
# format, not something meant to be hand-diffed) — project.yml is the real
# source of truth and is the only one tracked here.
/Rerack.xcodeproj/

## Build artifacts
build/
DerivedData/
*.o
*.LinkFileList

## Xcode per-user state (never shared, machine-specific)
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.xcscmblueprint

## Swift Package Manager
.build/
.swiftpm/

## Simulator / misc
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip
*.dSYM
*.xcarchive

## Signing & secrets — nothing here has ever been committed (verified), these
## are guards for things that would be easy to add by accident later.
##
## NOTE ON WHAT IS *NOT* SECRET: the Team ID in project.yml
## (DEVELOPMENT_TEAM) is deliberately tracked. A Team ID isn't a credential —
## it ships inside every distributed app binary and is needed for the project
## to build at all. The private keys below are the actual secrets.
*.p8
*.p12
*.pem
*.key
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
AuthKey_*.p8

## Environment / config secrets (relevant once V2's backend exists — PRD §12.5)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.json
Secrets.swift
*.secrets

